{number: 167}
{title: Surely Goodness and Mercy}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
A [D] mind of peace and rest is mine,
A [G] table rich and [D] free;
With holy oil my head is crowned,
My [A7] cup runs over me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Surely [D] goodness and mercy shall [G] follow me
All the [D] days of my [A7] life;
Surely [D] goodness and mercy shall [G] follow me
All the [D] days of my [A7] life;
And I shall [D] dwell in the house of the [G] Lord for-[D] ever,
And I shall feast at the table spread for [A7] me;
Surely [D] goodness and mercy shall [G] follow me
All the [D] days, all the [A7] days of my [D] life.
{end_of_chorus}
